anya: quick question about streaming contract — I'm proposing an optional `delta.type` field on stream frames to make it explicit what the chunk is ("text", "tool_call_start", "tool_call_chunk", "tool_call_end"). idea is it's omitted for pure text by default to avoid breaking. example frame:

```json
{
  "delta": {"type": "tool_call_chunk", "content": "{\"name\":\"search\",\"args\":\"{\\\"q\\\":\\\"foo\\\"}\"}"}
}
```

concerns: some SDKs currently treat every chunk as raw text and don't ignore unknown keys. should we: (a) omit `delta.type` unless non-text, (b) ship a response header `X-Streaming-Schema: 1.2` and opt-in flag in SDKs, or (c) bump schema and announce deprecation? @mike @ronnie thoughts?

mike: +1 on being conservative. my preference is (a) omit the field for pure text frames and only send it when frame semantics differ. also add a header (b) so newer clients can opt-in. i don't love a hard schema bump without an opt-in window — too many private runtimes.

ronnie: agreed — for function calls we should be explicit about boundaries. current behavior streams `content` with role=assistant and then a final function_call payload. new proposal should emit clear `function_call` subframes so clients can assemble args without guessing. we should also include an explicit `end` marker for multi-part function_arg streaming. minimal change: send `delta.type` only for non-text and include `fragment_index` for ordering if needed.

ivy: i opened a draft PR: https://github.com/redwood/inference/pull/2432 — adds the server flag + header + example client changes. it sets header `X-Streaming-Schema: 1.2` and a server-side feature flag `stream_delta_types`. default off in prod for 2 weeks, enable on staging. also added doc to api/streaming.md.

deploy-bot: deploy notice: deployed branch `streaming-type-flag` to staging at 2025-11-05T14:02:10Z :rocket:

anya: nice, thanks @ivy. a few clarifications before we iterate: (1) behavior for SDKs that buffer and concatenate — they should treat text frames exactly as before. (2) for function_call streaming: server will emit `tool_call_start` with metadata, then zero+ `tool_call_chunk` frames with `content`, and final `tool_call_end` with `metadata.complete = true`. (3) we will NOT change existing `role` or `content` fields.

mike: please add a unit test in runtime that simulates a naive client which concatenates all `delta.content` ignoring unknown fields — that should still produce the same reconstructed text for pure text streams. i'll add an integration test for function_call assembly.

ronnie: note for private deployments: we need a rollout page describing how older agents handle new headers/flags. i'll draft a short checklist: toggle feature flag, run compatibility tests, enable header-based clients gradually.

ivy: adding changelog entry and endpoint note. also adding a small migration snippet for on-prem: `sudo rictl set feature streaming-type --off && ./compat-check.sh` to validate.

anya: perfect. action items: [mike] review PR + add integration test, [ronnie] draft rollout doc for private, [ivy] finish changelog + set default off in prod for 2w, i'll merge after approvals. leaving a short example for docs (feel free to copy):

```json
// text frame (unchanged)
{
  "delta": { "content": "hello"} 
}

// function call frames (new, optional)
{
  "delta": { "type": "tool_call_start", "metadata": {"name": "search"}}
}
{
  "delta": { "type": "tool_call_chunk", "content": "{\"q\":\"foo\"}"}
}
{
  "delta": { "type": "tool_call_end", "metadata": {"complete": true}}
}
```

mike: i'll take it on today, ping me in PR comments if urgent.

ronnie: i'll put a draft rollout doc in `docs/ops/rollouts/streaming-delta.md` and ping infra.

ivy: pushed changelog and tests to the PR, awaiting reviews.

anya: thanks team :thumbsup: closing the loop here — will merge once approvals + CI green.
